      "hints": [
        "Angle $BDO$ has vertex $D$: find $\\overrightarrow{DB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{DO}$, or reverse both.",
        "Use $D=E+7\\mathbf{k}$ and $B=8\\mathbf{i}+6\\mathbf{j}$ to form those vectors.",
        "Compute their dot product, both lengths, and the inverse cosine."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{OD}=(1.6,1.2,7)$ and $\\overrightarrow{BD}=\\overrightarrow{OD}-\\overrightarrow{OB}=(-6.4,-4.8,7)$. Reversing both gives the angle at $D$.",
        "$\\overrightarrow{OD}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{BD}=1.6(-6.4)+1.2(-4.8)+7^2=33$. Also $|OD|=\\sqrt{53}$ and $|BD|=\\sqrt{113}$.",
        "$\\cos\\angle BDO=\\frac{33}{\\sqrt{53}\\sqrt{113}}$, so $\\angle BDO=64.8^\\circ$ (3 s.f.)."
      ],
